      "message": "For reference:\n\nWe enter move_queued_task with only rq-\u003elock held, and we should leave with cpu_rq(new_cpu)-\u003elock held.\n\nSince we have WALT and will call walt_fixup_busy_time for a migration inside set_task_cpu, we need to ensure that we hold the rq-\u003elock for both CPUs if they are different.\n\ndouble_lock_balance will handle the case where the two locks are the same one since it eventually calls double_rq_lock which is OK with this.\n\nThe error we saw after the previous change occurs when both CPUs are the same. What happens is that we unlock new_rq in the double_unlock_balance and then unconditionally unlock rq-\u003elock which (in this case) is the same one we just unlocked.\n\nIt seems to me that using double_rq_unlock here directly accomplishes exactly what we need.",
